00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:18.830
You caught some!

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:20.660
They caught some.

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:23.660
Maybe I should've invited Natsumi, too.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:29.540
But it'd be nice if I caught a lot
and send her a picture to surprise her.

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.580
Okay, I think I'll fish here.

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:36.450
All right, all set. Now, I just need the bait.

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:37.370
"Just Give It a Squeeze"
"For <i>sabiki </i>fishing"
All right, all set. Now, I just need the bait.

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:37.830
All right, all set. Now, I just need the bait.

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:42.540
Why don't we use this all
the time? It's so convenient.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:45.040
Thanks for telling me about it, Mr. Owner.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:47.000
Yeah!

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:48.580
There!

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:54.700
Here they come.
They're gobbling up the bait.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.120
Now, I just need to wait for the tug.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.120
Just waiting for the tug... The tug...

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.330
Huh?

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.870
Well, I guess that might
happen once in a while.

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:07.290
I'll shake the rod up and down
to spread the bait a bit more.

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:09.830
Good, good, good, good, good!

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:11.700
Why, though?!

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:18.410
Usually, I barely have to do
anything to catch some.

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:24.040
Dang it. You insolent li'l horsies!
I'm gonna catch you, no matter what!

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:34.410
There we go!

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.750
Yes! I finally caught one...?!

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:48.080
Why? What am I doing wrong?

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.580
Maybe I'll just go home...

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:56.500
"Incoming Call"
"Natsumi Hodaka"

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:58.750
Hello?

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:01.540
Hey, Hina. What are you doing right now?

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:03.250
I'm fishing for li'l horsies.

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:06.450
Seriously?! Why didn't you invite me?

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:10.250
Sorry... But I haven't been able to catch any.

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:12.410
Where are you fishing at?

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:15.450
The place near my house
with the really long breakwater.

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:19.080
There, huh? Okay, I'll be right there!

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:22.450
Huh? She hung up.

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:32.290
There you are.

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:33.910
Huh?!

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:36.370
You scared me! You're way too fast!

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:39.080
Well, my house is right over there.

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:41.870
You should've invited me, jeez.
I was so bored I was just lazing around,

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:44.410
playing video games with my little brother.

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:47.620
I wanted to catch a lot and surprise you.

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:52.370
What? You've got at least ten more
years before you can surprise me.

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:53.540
What's your rig look like?

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:55.080
Here you go.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:58.040
Wait, this is a seven or an eight.

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:59.410
A seven?

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:03.700
The size of the hooks.
Wasn't it listed on the bag?

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:07.120
Oh, you're right. It says seven.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:10.660
Those hooks are way too big,
so it won't fit in their mouths.

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:13.160
Use these twos instead.

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:16.080
Wow, they're totally different in size.

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:18.830
We always use two.

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:20.700
Oh, we do?

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.950
You should know what size we use by now.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:26.330
Also, this rod is probably
for octopus fishing.

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:29.040
They're made to be sturdy, so you
can pry an octopus that's sticking

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:32.250
onto a surface with its suckers,
so they also don't bend when you shake them.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:33.870
Huh...

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:35.700
Horse mackerels have weak mouths,

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:39.620
so more flexible rods help absorb
the impact of them being pulled up

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:41.950
and the hook doesn't let go as easily.

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:45.250
The sturdier the rod,
the less impact they'll absorb,

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:47.540
and the hooks come off easier.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:49.160
No wonder.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:51.200
Here you go. Try fishing with this one.

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:53.500
Thanks.

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.790
I wonder if this will really work...

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:58.200
I can see the doubt in your face.

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:04.000
See?

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.830
I'm sorry I doubted you!

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:08.450
So you did doubt me!

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:16.580
What's up?

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:18.910
I'm having a hard time getting the hook off.

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:21.950
Hold onto the hook and flip it.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:26.750
I did it!

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.660
It's amazing though.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:34.620
All we did was change the
hook size and we caught this many.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:38.370
Well, there's a reason
that there're different rigs.

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:44.200
I guess I wasn't really thinking
about anything when I was fishing.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:48.120
Well, you didn't know any better.
You just started fishing.

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:52.410
You can continue making plenty of
mistakes and learning from them.

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:55.250
Not to mention, you can use the exact same rig

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:59.700
tomorrow and not be able to
catch a thing and have no idea why.

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:02.200
So you don't need to worry about it.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.330
But you know...

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:13.700
...I'm having a blast,
even with all that in mind.

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:19.000
Yeah.

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:25.290
Want me to help you carry all that home?

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:27.790
It's fine. It's just around the corner.

00:21:27.790 --> 00:21:30.500
Thanks for your help today.

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:33.290
I shall guide you again, my student.

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:38.910
I'll keep doing my best so
I can be the teacher someday.

00:21:38.910 --> 00:21:42.500
It's really frustrating having
Natsumi teach me for some reason.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:49.290
Welcome home! You get a huge haul?

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:50.540
I'm home...

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:54.370
I need to worry about being
able to haul myself around first...

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:58.250
Today's haiku...

00:21:58.250 --> 00:21:59.750
"Make sure you always

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.330
wash off any and all krill

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:02.830
before you head home."

00:22:02.830 --> 00:22:04.370
By Hina.
